    "risks": [
      "If managers quietly treat home days as less committed, or pull people in on Wednesdays and Fridays 'when needed,' staff will see the promise of unchanged reviews and promotion as hollow, and the retention gain could erode. The managers modelled are the least invested in the policy.",
      "The policy does not address career drivers. About 489 people are still predicted to leave, and voices like 'I'm still going to be asking about promotion timing' and 'it won't make me stay forever' show that pay and progression remain the deciding factors for many.",
      "Expectations may ratchet up. Several employees already say they want 'more flexibility eventually,' so the goodwill may fade as two days becomes the new baseline, and any later rollback would likely hurt more than never offering it."
    ],
